## RAW TEST OUTPUT (verbatim, produced by the orchestrator before review)

Command: bash test/serve.py (stdlib http.server honouring vercel.json redirects+headers), then curl -sSI http://127.0.0.1:8899/<path>
Result: every declared header is actually sent, and Cache-Control splits correctly:

    HTTP/1.0 200 OK
    Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https://cdn.donmai.us; media-src 'self' https://www.soundhelix.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com; script-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://cdn.jsdelivr.net; connect-src 'self'
    X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
    Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
    Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=(), usb=()
    Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload
    X-DNS-Prefetch-Control: off
    Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400

    $ curl -sSI http://127.0.0.1:8899/Project/assets/css/script.css | grep -i cache-control
    Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, s-maxage=604800, stale-while-revalidate=86400
    Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

Path status codes (local, post-fix). Before the fix /fivefloors/ and /roomfall/ returned
404 on the live site, verified by curl against https://www.lyravein.my.id:

    /                              200
    /fivefloors/                   200
    /roomfall/                     200
    /denia/                        200
    /Project/                      200
    /robots.txt                    200
    /sitemap.xml                   200
    /.well-known/security.txt      200

Browser check (headless Chrome via CDP) that the strict CSP does not break rendering:
font-family resolved to "Outfit, sans-serif" on all four public pages, body
backgrounds rendered, 1 stylesheet + 1 inline script present per page.
One image did not load (cdn.donmai.us hero on /denia/). Isolated as NOT a CSP
problem: with the policy replaced by `default-src * data: blob: 'unsafe-inline'
'unsafe-eval'; ...` the same image still failed with responseStatus 0 and
naturalWidth 0, while `curl` from the host fetched it with code 200. The sandboxed
browser cannot reach that CDN.

Line-ending discipline check: the two renamed files keep their original endings
(fivefloors CRLF, roomfall LF). Verified by stripping CRLF and dropping the
inserted meta lines, then hashing: both files hash identical to their pre-change
content (68fd6884b7304321 and 91a130c5acac5609).
